      "term": "Wanli work strike",
      "definition": "Historians' name for the Wanli Emperor's decades-long withdrawal from governing (roughly 1589–1620), during which he refused to attend court, fill vacant offices, or act on most memorials — leaving the Ming state to run on institutional autopilot."
